# Committed on purpose — these are build-time, client-visible values, not
# secrets. Vite loads this automatically for production builds (`vite build`
# uses production mode). Real secrets (Stripe, Supabase service role, etc.)
# stay in the deploy environment's Secrets panel, never here.
#
# Generate is off by default everywhere (see src/lib/generation/feature-flag.ts).
# This alone flips it for BOTH the client and the server bundle, because Vite
# statically inlines import.meta.env.VITE_* into every bundle it builds,
# server included. Also set GENERATION_ENABLED=true (no VITE_ prefix) as a
# real Secret in the deploy environment — the server's own process.env
# fallback reads that name, and Lovable's Secrets panel will accept it since
# it isn't VITE_-prefixed. Setting only one of the two produces a client/
# server mismatch: SSR renders "Generate" while the hydrated client bundle
# still thinks it's off.
VITE_GENERATION_ENABLED=true
